on framing a reusable representation for organizing assumptions, variables, and relationships before analysis begins. As the final topic in this module, cash-flow diagrams carries the completed idea into interest and equivalence."}]}, {"id": "55283af9-1b85-420b-b5aa-4a56c62f31be", "type": "topic", "title": "Interest and equivalence", "description": "This module builds directly on decision framing and develops interest and equivalence. It belongs here because its methods and distinctions are prerequisites for uniform and gradient series.", "children": [{"id": "fce497e9-ceda-417b-b25c-50db17ce66e0", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Simple vs compound interest", "children": [], "description": "Simple vs compound interest identifies a specific object, distinction, or relationship within interest and equivalence. Learners need to recognize and use it before combining this module's ideas in later work. It appears before effective rates because that next topic assumes this starting point."}, {"id": "5ef199fc-f27d-4661-a92f-0f89cb4b83df", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Effective rates", "children": [], "description": "Effective rates identifies a specific object, distinction, or relationship within interest and equivalence. Learners need to recognize and use it before combining this module's ideas in later work. After simple vs compound interest, effective rates supplies what is needed to address present and future worth."}, {"id": "8dca51fc-cd65-4f18-9cfd-0a18078a02fb", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Present and future worth", "children": [], "description": "Present and future worth identifies a specific object, distinction, or relationship within interest and equivalence. Learners need to recognize and use it before combining this module's ideas in later work. As the final topic in this module, present and future worth carries the completed idea into uniform and gradient series."}]}, {"id": "dc078eba-f430-4b1f-8aaf-1d9615f5a1b5", "type": "topic", "title": "Uniform and gradient series", "description": "This module builds directly on interest and equivalence and develops uniform and gradient series. It belongs here because its methods and distinctions are prerequisites for rate conversions.", "children": [{"id": "0814bc81-eaa9-4270-9d81-5a193b2b224d", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Annuities", "children": [], "description": "Annuities identifies a specific object, distinction, or relationship within uniform and gradient series. Learners need to recognize and use it before combining this module's ideas in later work. It appears before arithmetic gradients because that next topic assumes this starting point."}, {"id": "519c0760-71e5-41bd-9b81-080bde98a7df", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Arithmetic gradients", "children": [], "description": "Arithmetic gradients identifies a specific object, distinction, or relationship within uniform and gradient series. Learners need to recognize and use it before combining this module's ideas in later work. After annuities, arithmetic gradients supplies what is needed to address geometric gradients."}, {"id": "0e4dd5d7-4e92-4cb7-b1d0-f20a705d4d31", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Geometric gradients", "children": [], "description": "Geometric gradients identifies a specific object, distinction, or relationship within uniform and gradient series. Learners need to recognize and use it before combining this module's ideas in later work. As the final topic in this module, geometric gradients carries the completed idea into rate conversions."}]}, {"id": "176fe6d6-4a58-45ce-943c-b6766a7fdd92", "type": "topic", "title": "Rate conversions", "description": "This module builds directly on uniform and gradient series and develops rate conversions. It belongs here because its methods and distinctions are prerequisites for project comparison.", "children": [{"id": "84cedcd1-7876-4204-af7f-978e40cf4678", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Nominal vs effective", "children": [], "description": "Nominal vs effective identifies a specific object, distinction, or relationship within rate conversions. Learners need to recognize and use it before combining this module's ideas in later work. It appears before compounding periods because that next topic assumes this starting point."}, {"id": "c0dfc564-d391-4e0e-8bcb-b09310239485", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Compounding periods", "children": [], "description": "Compounding periods identifies a specific object, distinction, or relationship within rate conversions. Learners need to recognize and use it before combining this module's ideas in later work. After nominal vs effective, compounding periods supplies what is needed to address continuous compounding."}, {"id": "e9fabf6a-23e9-420e-a5b2-5411cf22c83f", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Continuous compounding", "children": [], "description": "Continuous compounding identifies a specific object, distinction, or relationship within rate conversions. Learners need to recognize and use it before combining this module's ideas in later work. As the final topic in this module, continuous compounding carries the completed idea into project comparison."}]}, {"id": "0b800387-584e-4b7f-b138-6fc39f1ca44c", "type": "topic", "title": "Project comparison", "description": "This module builds directly on rate conversions and develops project comparison. It belongs here because its methods and distinctions are prerequisites for rate-of-return methods.", "children": [{"id": "1480fcb9-9c63-48f0-9ed0-2c5f083bc474", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Present worth", "children": [], "description": "Present worth identifies a specific object, distinction, or relationship within project comparison. Learners need to recognize and use it before combining this module's ideas in later work. It appears before annual worth because that next topic assumes this starting point."}, {"id": "14a0828b-83b6-4b73-9958-b19b4b78746e", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Annual worth", "children": [], "description": "Annual worth identifies a specific object, distinction, or relationship within project comparison. Learners need to recognize and use it before combining this module's ideas in later work. After present worth, annual worth supplies what is needed to address future worth."}, {"id": "cfd9cbfb-7b64-4b7a-a4cb-3eba4dcb2a35", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Future worth", "children": [], "description": "Future worth identifies a specific object, distinction, or relationship within project comparison. Learners need to recognize and use it before combining this module's ideas in later work. After annual worth, future worth supplies what is needed to address study periods."}, {"id": "061faacf-14c3-42a5-8282-067b6961889c", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Study periods", "children": [], "description": "Study periods identifies a specific object, distinction, or relationship within project comparison. Learners need to recognize and use it before combining this module's ideas in later work. As the final topic in this module, study periods carries the completed idea into rate-of-return methods."}]}, {"id": "bd36acad-7b84-47f2-81b5-e45a536ff2d0", "type": "topic", "title": "Rate-of-return methods", "description": "This module builds directly on project comparison and develops rate-of-return methods. It belongs here because its methods and distinctions are prerequisites for benefit–cost analysis.", "children": [{"id": "6c70a48c-f5c2-4a50-9562-03dca32e8476", "type": "subtopic", "title": "IRR", "children": [], "description": "IRR identifies a specific object, distinction, or relationship within rate-of-return methods. Learners need to recognize and use it before combining this module's ideas in later work. It appears before incremental analysis because that next topic assumes this starting point."}, {"id": "9ec0503d-a3b8-4d6e-8784-6cd3f37c62b2", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Incremental analysis", "children": [], "description": "Incremental analysis identifies a specific object, distinction, or relationship within rate-of-return methods. Learners need to recognize and use it before combining this module's ideas in later work. After irr, incremental analysis supplies what is needed to address multiple-rate pitfalls."}, {"id": "734f45bb-c11a-4057-b8ea-2e6bab69dcbb", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Multiple-rate pitfalls", "children": [], "description": "Multiple-rate pitfalls identifies a specific object, distinction, or relationship within rate-of-return methods. Learners need to recognize and use it before combining this module's ideas in later work. After incremental analysis, multiple-rate pitfalls supplies what is needed to address err."}, {"id": "d37ece37-f937-46c0-a276-0efff2c12d1f", "type": "subtopic", "title": "ERR", "children": [], "description": "ERR identifies a specific object, distinction, or relationship within rate-of-return methods. Learners need to recognize and use it before combining this module's ideas in later work. As the final topic in this module, err carries the completed idea into benefit–cost analysis."}]}, {"id": "596a2769-9d82-44b8-bb8d-dc7404763c58", "type": "topic", "title": "Benefit–cost analysis", "description": "This module builds directly on rate-of-return methods and develops benefit–cost analysis. It belongs here because its methods and distinctions are prerequisites for depreciation and taxes.", "children": [{"id": "3c126194-9a12-452b-a9f3-c9f6acb50089", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Public projects", "children": [], "description": "Public projects identifies a specific object, distinction, or relationship within benefit–cost analysis. Learners need to recognize and use it before combining this module's ideas in later work. It appears before mutually exclusive alternatives because that next topic assumes this starting point."}, {"id": "5e497b3f-ae73-427e-9282-9aac4e04ac90", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Mutually exclusive alternatives", "children": [], "description": "Mutually exclusive alternatives identifies a specific object, distinction, or relationship within benefit–cost analysis. Learners need to recognize and use it before combining this module's ideas in later work. After public projects, mutually exclusive alternatives supplies what is needed to address ranking conflicts."}, {"id": "65faefaf-4570-4b2b-a920-aaf4e5427a5b", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Ranking conflicts", "children": [], "description": "Ranking conflicts identifies a specific object, distinction, or relationship within benefit–cost analysis. Learners need to recognize and use it before combining this module's ideas in later work. As the final topic in this module, ranking conflicts carries the completed idea into depreciation and taxes."}]}, {"id": "dfe76bca-f847-42db-9aa6-6ec3f9499cfd", "type": "topic", "title": "Depreciation and taxes", "description": "This module builds directly on benefit–cost analysis and develops depreciation and taxes. It belongs here because its methods and distinctions are prerequisites for replacement decisions.", "children": [{"id": "8944c9de-3b21-47dc-b5f5-54b0e6c5aa83", "type": "subtopic", "title": "MACRS", "children": [], "description": "MACRS identifies a specific object, distinction, or relationship within depreciation and taxes. Learners need to recognize and use it before combining this module's ideas in later work. It appears before book value because that next topic assumes this starting point."}, {"id": "3018d2b1-df32-4688-ac43-2263272ade8c", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Book value", "children": [], "description": "Book value identifies a specific object, distinction, or relationship within depreciation and taxes. Learners need to recognize and use it before combining this module's ideas in later work. After macrs, book value supplies what is needed to address after-tax cash flow."}, {"id": "2ed90a60-3fbb-4a43-a290-c3ffd9c57171", "type": "subtopic", "title": "After-tax cash flow", "children": [], "description": "After-tax cash flow identifies a specific object, distinction, or relationship within depreciation and taxes. Learners need to recognize and use it before combining this module's ideas in later work. After book value, after-tax cash flow supplies what is needed to address capital gains."}, {"id": "ea1cb0ae-8f4a-42b4-af74-f5ecf09a63d3", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Capital gains", "children": [], "description": "Capital gains identifies a specific object, distinction, or relationship within depreciation and taxes. Learners need to recognize and use it before combining this module's ideas in later work. As the final topic in this module, capital gains carries the completed idea into replacement decisions."}]}, {"id": "f0dbddf0-3113-4de2-95ea-2987376582eb", "type": "topic", "title": "Replacement decisions", "description": "This module builds directly on depreciation and taxes and develops replacement decisions. It belongs here because its methods and distinctions are prerequisites for inflation and price change.", "children": [{"id": "0715a7f2-e113-4c30-9384-76194f322fb5", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Defender/challenger", "children": [], "description": "Defender/challenger identifies a specific object, distinction, or relationship within replacement decisions. Learners need to recognize and use it before combining this module's ideas in later work. It appears before economic life because that next topic assumes this starting point."}, {"id": "6b10d479-944a-418e-bff5-b547928c9f05", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Economic life", "children": [], "description": "Economic life identifies a specific object, distinction, or relationship within replacement decisions. Learners need to recognize and use it before combining this module's ideas in later work. After defender/challenger, economic life supplies what is needed to address sunk costs."}, {"id": "3e53d015-0e79-4d5b-aca6-b2d31cf7a70e", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Sunk costs", "children": [], "description": "Sunk costs identifies a specific object, distinction, or relationship within replacement decisions. Learners need to recognize and use it before combining this module's ideas in later work. After economic life, sunk costs supplies what is needed to address abandonment."}, {"id": "ae08886d-726a-4307-90fb-75301edd417b", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Abandonment", "children": [], "description": "Abandonment identifies a specific object, distinction, or relationship within replacement decisions. Learners need to recognize and use it before combining this module's ideas in later work. As the final topic in this module, abandonment carries the completed idea into inflation and price change."}]}, {"id": "ae039211-cca7-43f0-ae83-5078359ba0df", "type": "topic", "title": "Inflation and price change", "description": "This module builds directly on replacement decisions and develops inflation and price change. It belongs here because its methods and distinctions are prerequisites for uncertainty and risk.", "children": [{"id": "6d12cfbb-03b2-4453-8bd8-79c1d93a567e", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Real vs nominal dollars", "children": [], "description": "Real vs nominal dollars identifies a specific object, distinction, or relationship within inflation and price change. Learners need to recognize and use it before combining this module's ideas in later work. It appears before price indices because that next topic assumes this starting point."}, {"id": "15aa392f-c31c-44f8-a349-f04d89a87b17", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Price indices", "children": [], "description": "Price indices identifies a specific object, distinction, or relationship within inflation and price change. Learners need to recognize and use it before combining this module's ideas in later work. After real vs nominal dollars, price indices supplies what is needed to address mixed inflation rates."}, {"id": "0c030a87-0f17-4c42-a500-f44c722c2c8c", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Mixed inflation rates", "children": [], "description": "Mixed inflation rates identifies a specific object, distinction, or relationship within inflation and price change. Learners need to recognize and use it before combining this module's ideas in later work. As the final topic in this module, mixed inflation rates carries the completed idea into uncertainty and risk."}]}, {"id": "1ee73d54-f39c-4c9e-9246-8de77bfa5b68", "type": "topic", "title": "Uncertainty and risk", "description": "This module builds directly on inflation and price change and develops uncertainty and risk. It belongs here because its methods and distinctions are prerequisites for capital budgeting synthesis.", "children": [{"id": "35dc38ec-581a-49d4-a1c4-5b2f71c107ae", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Sensitivity", "children": [], "description": "Sensitivity makes the validity limits of uncertainty and risk explicit, showing when an otherwise correct method or system can become unreliable. It appears before break-even because that next topic assumes this starting point."}, {"id": "0030d855-cf23-4578-88f0-6e0ea97a032c", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Break-even", "children": [], "description": "Break-even identifies a specific object, distinction, or relationship within uncertainty and risk. Learners need to recognize and use it before combining this module's ideas in later work. After sensitivity, break-even supplies what is needed to address scenarios."}, {"id": "b1425cbf-6fa3-4530-9b0a-3dab9f7455d0", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Scenarios", "children": [], "description": "Scenarios identifies a specific object, distinction, or relationship within uncertainty and risk. Learners need to recognize and use it before combining this module's ideas in later work. After break-even, scenarios supplies what is needed to address expected value."}, {"id": "bb050173-49ef-461a-96ba-6c25b02d1a2f", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Expected value", "children": [], "description": "Expected value identifies a specific object, distinction, or relationship within uncertainty and risk. Learners need to recognize and use it before combining this module's ideas in later work. After scenarios, expected value supplies what is needed to address monte carlo concepts."}, {"id": "93224303-3fc8-4980-90b4-6720711b8f85", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Monte Carlo concepts", "children": [], "description": "Monte Carlo concepts identifies a specific object, distinction, or relationship within uncertainty and risk. Learners need to recognize and use it before combining this module's ideas in later work. As the final topic in this module, monte carlo concepts carries the completed idea into capital budgeting synthesis."}]}, {"id": "ee11ab58-0272-4915-98a0-4822351faf4d", "type": "topic", "title": "Capital budgeting synthesis", "description": "This culminating module draws on uncertainty and risk and develops capital budgeting synthesis. It belongs last because it requires the earlier tools to be selected, combined, and evaluated rather than used one at a time.", "children": [{"id": "fb4b8809-927b-4c79-b0a7-7e452c1de454", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Financing assumptions", "children": [], "description": "Financing assumptions identifies a specific object, distinction, or relationship within capital budgeting synthesis. Learners need to recognize and use it before combining this module's ideas in later work. It appears before nonfinancial criteria because that next topic assumes this starting point."}, {"id": "a25ed7e9-25aa-4acd-89bf-1695ed9ac597", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Nonfinancial criteria", "children": [], "description": "Nonfinancial criteria identifies a specific object, distinction, or relationship within capital budgeting synthesis. Learners need to recognize and use it before combining this module's ideas in later work. After financing assumptions, nonfinancial criteria supplies what is needed to address recommendation memo."}, {"id": "5d2db375-1ff8-4835-9ac5-091e2cf5d3b7", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Recommendation memo", "children": [], "description": "Recommendation memo identifies a specific object, distinction, or relationship within capital budgeting synthesis. Learners need to recognize and use it before combining this module's ideas in later work. As the final course topic, recommendation memo requires ideas from the complete path to be integrated and transferred."}]}], "dbBacked": true}$engeconzzjs$::jsonb,
